"――Got a tiny little minute, pretty boy? Wanna talk with ya... jus' the two of us."

Called out to in the corridor, Subaru turned around, only to see 'Black Dog' standing before him.

Having finished their talk with Melty, who had then parted ways to head toward Russell, Subaru and Beatrice had been on their way to check on Crusch, who had fallen into a deep sleep from the exhaustion of battle.

And right then, 'Black Dog' appeared at a timing that made it feel like an ambush――

"Wait, isn't it actually an ambush? Were you waiting for us?"

"What's with that stunned, shocked look on your mug? Surprised and astounded and just can't believe I didn't barge into your little sit-down with 'White Sheep'?"

"Actually, yeah. Didn't know you were capable of holding your horses or reading the room."

"Well ain't that a flattering, uncalled-for review. Thanks a bunch. So, what's your answer to my offer?"

"My answer to just the two of us? I don't really mind, but..."

Saying that, Subaru raised the hand he was holding with Beatrice's.

They had only just suffered an attempt to isolate them during the battle with the 'Beloved Children'. Considering the mana consumption and the need to replenish his Beatromin, he didn't want to be separated from her right now.

"So, I'm with Beako, which means just the two of us is impossible. At best, being generous, you're getting two point five."

"Which of us are you counting as half a person, I suppose? To begin with, Betty's reliability when paired with Subaru is on the level of a hundred men, in fact."

"Heard that? That being the case, it's gonna be just the hundred and two of us. It'll be a whisper session with a pretty big crowd, but if that's fine by you, we'll keep you company."

"Thanks a ton for the sophistry and quibbling. Fine by me, fine by me. Better to count you two as a set right from the start than have a hundred people tattling on me. Desirable, even. Understood."

The word tattling made it sound like he was doing something bad, which pricked his conscience, but it would also be a shame to throw cold water on 'Black Dog' now that he was in the mood to talk. And so, taking advantage of the empty hallway, Subaru continued speaking with 'Black Dog' alongside Beatrice.

At any rate, what 'Black Dog' had gone out of his way to ambush them for was――

"――You already heard this and that and whatever else from 'White Sheep', didn't ya? The whole story of how and why we ended up working under that unsavory bastard."

"A lot of it didn't make sense, though. Melty-chan herself was troubled by how moth-eaten her memories are. But we heard the most important part. ――Her desire, and her resolve."

"And Betty and Subaru promised to lend a hand, I suppose."

"Oh, how kind, how broad-minded. Good for you. Breaking through that distrust of people, huh?"

A distrust of people seemed ill-suited to Melty, yet it wasn't an entirely inaccurate assessment.

Born with the power of 'Bewitchment', Melty could never truly, deeply believe in the goodwill of others. Because she couldn't tell whether the kindness directed at her came from the person themselves, or was caused by her own power.

Whether distinguishing between the two had any meaning or not wasn't something outsiders had any business lightly debating. ――Perhaps that very frustration was something 'Black Dog' shared as well.

Either way, 'Black Dog' watched over Melty closely.

"Though, that makes 'Black Dog' seem even more..."

"Like a tragic man whose chances of being in a pitiful position just shot up, in fact."

"What's with those eyes from the two of ya?! Don't you go pitying people however you please! First off, 'White Sheep' and I ain't got that kinda relationship. Sure, when she's all mopey, it gets under my skin and makes me itch so bad I can't stand it."

""Staaaaare.""

"Knock it off, idiots, stop, that's not it! To me, 'White Sheep' is... yeah, like a pet. I get irritated when she won't take to training the way I want. I get these clever ideas of how things'd be better if she did this or did that, but she can't pull 'em off. So my hands and mouth just end up meddling."

"That sounds less like treating her like a pet, and more like..."

'Black Dog' wore a face as if he had successfully put their relationship into words, but to Subaru, it felt like a far warmer bond than a pet—something closer to a parent's perspective.

"――. We heard from Melty that you have neither 'memories' nor a 'name', I suppose. Is that the truth, in fact?"

As if stealing the topic away from the hesitating Subaru, Beatrice turned the question to 'Black Dog'. At that, 'Black Dog' waved both hands lightly.

"If ya mean that neither I nor anyone around me remembers who I was, then yeah. Hilarious, ain't it? No memory, no record of who or what I am. What, am I a newborn baby born this damn big?"

"That must be rough..."

Though 'Black Dog' took a clownish attitude, his solitary circumstances were probably closest to Rem's right after she woke up in Vollachia.

However, Rem had Subaru right beside her, someone who remembered who she was. While that in itself ended up causing plenty of friction with Rem due to how poorly Subaru handled things, the thought of Rem being cast out all alone into a situation without even that gave him chills.

And 'Black Dog' had been placed in just such a chilling, helpless position.

"You don't have any clues about yourself? Anything at all?"

"...Thanks to hookin' up with the 'Six Tongues', I figured out and got a hold of the fact that the Sin Archbishops of 'Gluttony' were involved, no doubt about it. But that's all. Might've been a different story if I could've talked with the captive 'Gluttony', but before a chance to meet the guy came around――"

"Roy was killed, huh. And after that, you've been working with us."

"Exaaaactly."

'Black Dog' made skilled use of modern phrasing, but the reality of lacking both 'memories' and a 'name' was perhaps the very reason he absorbed such knowledge so naturally.

At the same time that fleeting impression crossed his mind, Subaru frowned, murmuring, "Still."

"What did you want to talk about that made you set up this time? Is this a mutual understanding scene, where we learn about your circumstances too? That does kinda feel like it deepens our camaraderie, though."

"Ha! Camaraderie is a real good word, makes me wanna laugh and squirm. Sure, we're comrades, all right. ――Comrades bein' used however 'Silver Fox' pleases."

"...Used by Russell-san?"

With 'Black Dog' lowering his tone slightly, those words sounded entirely different from a mere reference to the two months they had been forced to travel with the 'Six Tongues'.

Naturally, Subaru was well aware that Russell was utilizing their positions and abilities. And Subaru's side had considered it mutual, in the sense that they were borrowing the strength of the 'Six Tongues'.

However――

"That bastard 'Silver Fox' is way, way, waaaay nastier than you guys think or imagine. The info he doles out to us, his pawns, is controlled carefully and thoroughly. For instance..."

"For instance?"

"That princess of yours you think is being a good girl in the castle? Apparently she ran away from the castle with another princess in the same boat. Now your whole camp is on the wanted list. He ain't told ya this and that about that, haaas he?"

"Wha... What?!"

At 'Black Dog's exaggerated tilt of the head and words, Subaru's eyes snapped wide in frozen shock.

Emilia, who was supposed to be under house arrest in Lugunica's royal castle in the capital. ――He hadn't really expected her to just sit quietly, but hearing that she had broken out was like a bolt out of the blue.

If she had broken out, that meant she had judged there was something she needed to run from. That was synonymous with danger closing in on her, and he needed to confirm her safety right――

"Calm down, I suppose, Subaru. ――'Black Dog', what is your proof for what you just said, in fact? Roswaal's friend 'Silver Fox' is questionable, but your position smells just as suspicious, I suppose."

"――! Beako."

With deliberate composure, Beatrice reined in Subaru's rising panic. In response to her question, 'Black Dog' said, "Whoa, whoa," tilting his head from side to side.

"Ain't you harsh, doubting me like that, squirt. Jus' a bit ago you were healing my wounds and sending me out to help 'Gray Star' and the others, weren't ya?"

"How one handles an emergency is different from normal times, in fact. Melty spoke from the heart, I suppose. It is high time you did the same, in fact."

"――. Right and unshakable, truuuly a sound argument."

Acknowledging Beatrice's clear rebuke, 'Black Dog' let his shoulders drop heavily. Then, lowering his hood back, he took off his mask and faced Subaru and Beatrice.

Seeing his rarely revealed real face bared before them, Subaru's eyes rounded.

"...What's with the sudden formality?"

"Pretty decent face, ain't it? 'Gray Star', being a sucker for good looks, might drool over it, but don't you go praising it or staring. I don't like this face. That's why I wear this thing."

Saying so, the unmasked 'Black Dog' twisted his lips into a crude smirk.

With wavy light brown hair and dark skin, 'Black Dog's bare face was that of a rugged, dauntless, handsome man. In the past two months, Subaru had caught glimpses of it several times during infiltration missions, but he could never quite get used to the gap between those features and the man's usual behavior.

Even now, without that bared-teeth, beast-like grin, he almost wouldn't recognize him.

"Is showing your face supposed to be your idea of sincerity, I suppose?"

"I ain't sayin' you gotta trust and believe me just 'cause I showed my face. Might have some effect on you guys, but the real reason's different. It's just easier to explain what's next."

"Explain what's next..."

"Put my mug aside for later. More importantly, the proof you wanna hear and know about. The info gathered from all over by the 'Six Tongues' ends up with 'Silver Fox'. And then that bastard picks and chooses what to feed to us. Got it so far?"

"That... I get. Russell-san definitely hasn't shown us his whole hand. But hiding something about Emilia crosses the line, no matter what."

Even if he was acting cold-blooded for the sake of the Kingdom, if he was doing that while knowing what Subaru and the others prioritized above all else, trust couldn't exist here.

Whether it was the truth or not, 'Black Dog' pulled a single folded piece of paper from inside his coat and showed it off.

"By the way, I found out about the princess by swiping a bird letter the guy loves to use. It's an insidious, persistent thing written in cipher with deception mixed in, but you can probably believe this part."

'Black Dog' fluttered the slip of paper in front of them.

A bird letter was essentially the equivalent of a carrier pigeon in this world, a communication method where specially trained birds carried letters that would burst into flames if not opened through the proper procedure or specified method. The 'Six Tongues' frequently made use of this method to streamline their exchange of information.

Naturally, intercepting or peeking at a bird letter of the 'Six Tongues' had to be among the most difficult feats in the Kingdom. If 'Black Dog' had managed to pull that off and obtain information, its credibility had to be high.

"I'll give ya this bird letter. Decipher it however you damn well please later, and use it to back up my words or whatever. Point is, 'Silver Fox' can't be trusted. But that's talk about his character, not saying every piece of info he holds is bunk."

"...I still don't see what you're trying to get at. You're not trying to get us on your side to stage some late protest for labor reforms. And getting your hands on this bird letter in the first place is weird."

"Weird? What's so strange and out-of-the-ordinary about it?"

"Because think about it. It's not like you just happened to pick up something that was dropped. Learning about Emilia's situation was just a side effect for you; you must have planned to peek at that bird letter because there was information you wanted for yourself. Which means..."

"――Quick on the uptake, nice rhythm. That's why you guys are just right, perfect fit."

In an instant, 'Black Dog's hand grabbed Subaru's shoulder, slamming his back against the corridor wall. Subaru's breath caught, and Beatrice's voice went shrill. "Subaru!"

She shoved her small body between Subaru and 'Black Dog' without missing a beat.

"What are you doing all of a sudden, in fact?! If you lay a hand on Subaru..."

"What're ya gonna do, huh? You just messed up earlier with that slow reaction time, didn't ya?"

"――Murak!"

Goaded by 'Black Dog', Beatrice gritted her teeth and activated her magic.

A faint light spread, affecting the body of 'Black Dog' as he pinned Subaru to the wall. It was meant to lighten his body, allowing even Beatrice to easily shove him away――

"――?! The effect vanished, I suppose?!"

"Khahaha, thanks for the meal!"

Responding to Beatrice's astonished cry with a laugh, 'Black Dog' brought his right hand to his mouth, caught the tip of the glove with his teeth, and pulled it off.

Immediately, with a soft pop, 'Black Dog' thrust his bared palm out for Subaru and Beatrice to see.

There――

"...An eye, on his palm?"

"An Evil Eye, in fact. What's more, judging by the effect just now..."

"That's right, it sucked up, absorbed, and swallowed your magic. It's what ya call the Evil Eye of 'Magic Absorption'. Naturally, inevitably, you can probably guess where I hail from, right?"

"――Faradar?"

"Bingo, correct, ding-dong-ding-dong! Probably, anyway!"

Taking a step back, 'Black Dog' waved his hand in that clownish manner of his.

On his waving palm, an eye boasting a greenish sclera and a reptilian pupil—an Evil Eye, as it was called—protruded with a bulging presence.

In other words, that sudden violent act just now had been――

"A demonstration just to show off your Evil Eye?! Say it like a normal person!"

"Jus' a tiny little surprise. First of all, to begin with, you're the ones at fault for letting your guard down. You do realize the enemy we're dealin' with is a squishy, shapeshifting monster, don't ya?"

"That and the justification for your tomfoolery just now are completely different matters, in fact! What's more, after all that effort to charge Subaru's mana, it was reduced again, I suppose!"

"And I got pumped up by that much. Count it as a stock and call it a win. Now, how much did I say up to where... Oh, right, yeah! The part where 'White Sheep' and I are from the same hometown. Maybe."

"Can't be helped, I guess, but you don't even have definitive proof for that, do you..."

'Black Dog's testimony lacked a certain conviction, but there was no helping it. ――At any rate, if 'Black Dog' was of the Evil Eye clan, the idea that Faradar, which they had just heard about from Melty, was also his hometown carried plenty of weight.

Furthermore, while it seemed both 'Black Dog' and Melty had fallen victim to 'Gluttony' during their time as 'Beloved Children', if the two of them had originally been a pair, it made sense that they were together.

The two had fallen victim to 'Gluttony' in the same place, and despite losing their 'memories' and 'names', they had formed a relationship close to what they had had before. ――No, perhaps it wasn't just that.

"Melty-chan and 'Black Dog', your eye colors are..."

Recalling the face of Melty, whom he had faced just moments ago, Subaru stared intently at 'Black Dog's golden eyes once again. He had already known they were the same color, but learning that they were both from the same hometown and of the Evil Eye clan added a whole new layer of emotion to it.

And that emotion brought with it the possibility that the two weren't just from the same village, but were far closer—perhaps even bound by blood.

If so, a lot of things about how the usual relationship between 'Black Dog' and Melty appeared fell neatly into place.

However, 'Black Dog' waved his hand, saying, "Stop that, stop that."

"Annoying and stupid. Listen, will ya? That ain't the story I wanna tell or have you hear. It's about Faradar, but that's actually something I don't want reachin' 'White Sheep's ears."

"...And that loops back to why you were waiting for us in the first place, huh."

"Yeah, took a roundabout detour, didn't I? Anyhow, that Faradar's supposed to be my hometown, buuut... it ain't there anymore, and everyone involved is probably dead."

"――! Why would something like that..."

"Why or how, this is just a deduction I cobbled together from the info I got my hands on. Apparently, the whole territory of Faradar fell into the hands of some scary folks. But somehow they lost track of what they originally meant to use it for, so they went and disposed of it, or so it seems."

Hearing 'Black Dog's nonchalant explanation, Subaru exchanged a glance with Beatrice.

Though 'Black Dog' spoke of the apparent destruction of his hometown with total detachment, his explanation was terribly uneven, just as he had prefaced by calling it a deduction.

"In the first place, what does losing track of its original purpose even mean?"

"There's a theory that the bastards were just too damn stupid and moronic, but there's another theory too. Originally, securing Faradar was for somebody's sake, but because everybody forgot about that somebody, a debt with no discernible reason was left behind... kinda thing."

"――. In other words, they were hostages to keep Melty-chan or you in check?"

"And when 'White Sheep' and I vanished, it became pointless, I guess. So, here's the thing. I got business with the bastard who disposed of that Faradar."

"...Don't tell me, revenge? When you don't even remember anything?"

Catching the person who disposed of Faradar and interrogating them. Seeking a clue, a lead that might connect to his own past—the reason such a mild thought didn't cross Subaru's mind was because of the ferocious expression he saw on 'Black Dog' right before him.

What dwelled in his golden eyes wasn't that of a petitioner chasing after his past, but something far more savage, filled with the dark flames of fury.

"A guy who doesn't remember anything has his own way of settling scores, even if he doesn't remember a thing. Fine by me if you don't get it, y'know? Nobody, not a single damn soul's gonna understand."

"...No."

"――?"

"I get it. Even if it's not complete, I get it."

Subaru, too, had once been in a position where he had lost his memories and become empty. To be fair, what Subaru had lost were his memories since coming to another world; he hadn't become a complete zero.

Even so, Subaru in that state had still had a spring from which his feelings welled up, and it was certain that the things built up within that emptiness had become the foundation driving him forward.

'Black Dog' was probably the same. ――He might have started at zero, but he wasn't at zero anymore.

"Why won't you tell that to Melty, in fact?"

"Whoa, whoa, I told ya, didn't I? She's from the same hometown. In o-ther wo-ords! She's in a position where she could have the exact same motive as me. Imagine if she woke up to thoughts of revenge. The reason to live I finally got all for myself'd be snatched away, wouldn't it?"

"...Well, I suppose I will let you have it that way."

"What's with this squirt? There's a limit to how cheeky a brat can get, y'know?"

Crossing her short arms and letting out a long sigh, Beatrice made 'Black Dog's cheek twitch. But there was probably no need to worry about him doing anything worse. ――It was nothing complicated. This confession was fundamentally the same as the one Subaru and Beatrice had just had with Melty.

Foul-mouthed, overbearing in attitude, and difficult to read through his clownish behavior, but this was 'Black Dog's own way of showing he trusted Subaru and the others. That was why he had talked. That was all it was.

"So, going around in circles, what's the bottom line? Beako and I are gonna take this bird letter and storm Russell-san's place, and you want to tag along and press him about Faradar while we're at it... or something like that?"

"Actually, with 'Verdant Radiance' taking a nap, now's the chance. In this castle where none of the other 'Six Tongues' have barged in, we could force 'Silver Fox' to spill his guts. Buuut, if I didn't tell you guys first, you'd panic and flap around, right? So that's why."

"I see. ...Right now, Melty-chan went to Russell-san's place, so if you don't want her hearing about Faradar, now isn't the time."

"We'll pick our moment, pick our moment! You kinda get what I mean, don'tcha!"

Whether he was thorough or short-sighted was difficult to discern, but he had shared important information, and in a way characteristic of him, he had shown his trust.

Changing their plan, they would head to Russell right away, but before that――

"I understand your feelings about wanting revenge. I'll cooperate as much as I can. So long as it doesn't go against Emilia's wishes, our objective, and our promise with Melty-chan."

"Saying it out loud makes it sound quite binding, in fact."

"Yeah, but it's binding because I want it to be..."

Piling 'Black Dog's share on top of that would only add to the weight of the chains, but this poor ability to pick and choose wasn't anything new. Acknowledging the weight while untangling them one by one was Subaru's way of navigating this other world.

"――――"

At Subaru's reply, 'Black Dog' cast his gaze down to the Evil Eye in his palm. ――Could that fleeting look crossing his eyes be nostalgia for the ruined homeland he had no recollection of?

Clenching his palm into a fist and severing his awareness from his own Evil Eye that had met his gaze, he declared.

The name of his foe. That was――

"――Sakura Element. That bastard dies by my hand, no matter what, guaranteed."

It was an expression of unwavering resolve, one directly at odds with Melty's vow to take back what was lost.
